{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016UHKJM2nomGzKFdwtq9D6W","type":"tool_result","content":"✓ QuantAgent-sfc [BUG] · Fix SQLite/JSONB type incompatibility in test suite   [● P1 · CLOSED]\nOwner: Federico Scheu · Type: bug\nCreated: 2026-04-18 · Updated: 2026-04-24\n\nDESCRIPTION\nconftest.py creates an in-memory SQLite engine for tests, but quantagent/models.py uses PostgreSQL JSONB type (in the Logs table). SQLAlchemy raises 'Compiler can't render element of type JSONB' at test collection time, producing 147 errors before a single test runs. This blocks the entire CI pipeline.\n\nAffected files:\n- tests/conftest.py — create_test_db() uses SQLite\n- quantagent/models.py — Logs table uses JSONB column\n\nOptions (pick one):\nA) Switch test DB engine to PostgreSQL using testcontainers or a local Docker instance. Cleanest, aligns test env with production.\nB) Replace JSONB with JSON in models.py — loses PostgreSQL-specific operators but removes the engine dependency.\nC) Override column type in SQLite-only conftest fixture.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA\npytest tests/ -v completes collection with 0 errors. At least 450 tests pass (current: 456 pass when JSONB errors are excluded). CI pipeline green.\n\nLABELS: openclaw:merged, openclaw:test_done, testing\n\nBLOCKS\n  ← ✓ QuantAgent-0b5: Integrate PositionMonitor into TradingScheduler ● P2\n\nCOMMENTS\n  2026-04-21 08:08 Federico Scheu\n    ### Skill: autodev-implementer\n    - **Resultado:** SUCCESS\n    - **Run-ID:** 20260418-223000Z","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3a60d591-fe5d-4de7-8290-31c37bcbd12c","uuid":"3bb4c4ab-f28c-4666-9e68-bd464435aa2a","timestamp":"2026-05-04T17:41:33.236Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"✓ QuantAgent-sfc [BUG] · Fix SQLite/JSONB type incompatibility in test suite   [● P1 · CLOSED]\nOwner: Federico Scheu · Type: bug\nCreated: 2026-04-18 · Updated: 2026-04-24\n\nDESCRIPTION\nconftest.py creates an in-memory SQLite engine for tests, but quantagent/models.py uses PostgreSQL JSONB type (in the Logs table). SQLAlchemy raises 'Compiler can't render element of type JSONB' at test collection time, producing 147 errors before a single test runs. This blocks the entire CI pipeline.\n\nAffected files:\n- tests/conftest.py — create_test_db() uses SQLite\n- quantagent/models.py — Logs table uses JSONB column\n\nOptions (pick one):\nA) Switch test DB engine to PostgreSQL using testcontainers or a local Docker instance. Cleanest, aligns test env with production.\nB) Replace JSONB with JSON in models.py — loses PostgreSQL-specific operators but removes the engine dependency.\nC) Override column type in SQLite-only conftest fixture.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA\npytest tests/ -v completes collection with 0 errors. At least 450 tests pass (current: 456 pass when JSONB errors are excluded). CI pipeline green.\n\nLABELS: openclaw:merged, openclaw:test_done, testing\n\nBLOCKS\n  ← ✓ QuantAgent-0b5: Integrate PositionMonitor into TradingScheduler ● P2\n\nCOMMENTS\n  2026-04-21 08:08 Federico Scheu\n    ### Skill: autodev-implementer\n    - **Resultado:** SUCCESS\n    - **Run-ID:** 20260418-223000Z","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
